\abstract{
We present the STME-RS-A framework, a warped extra-dimensional model incorporating
quartic bulk anharmonicity. The resulting Kaluza--Klein (KK) spectrum exhibits
non-equidistant level spacing, providing a falsifiable geometric signature distinct
from standard Randall--Sundrum constructions. We derive the full Sturm--Liouville
structure, compute analytic approximations for the anharmonic mass shifts, and
construct collider-ready benchmark points (BP1--BP4). We further analyze production
cross sections, branching ratios, and exclusion contours for HL-LHC conditions at
$\sqrt{s}=13.6~\text{TeV}$ with $3~\text{ab}^{-1}$ of integrated luminosity.
}

